From d335007dea33dbdb54267d9ae601fe85755b8cd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:32:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Export GTK4 header bar menus to the global menu

Enabled by gtk-shell-shows-menubar, disabled with GTK_NOCSD_NO_GLOBAL_MENU=1

Assisted-by: LLM Claude Opus 5.5
---
 README.md          |   8 +
 Source/GTK-NoCSD.c | 883 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 890 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index b96a4c1..9b5faaa 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -145,12 +145,20 @@ The library supports some environment variables to influence its behavior:
 - `GTK_NOCSD_NO_CSS`: Setting to 1 disables loading any CSS from the library.
 - `GTK_NOCSD_NO_GTK3`: Setting to 1 disables the library for GTK3.
 - `GTK_NOCSD_NO_GTK4`: Setting to 1 disables the library for GTK4.
+- `GTK_NOCSD_NO_GLOBAL_MENU`: Setting to 1 disables exporting the header bar menu of GTK4 applications to the global menu.
 
 Make sure to set gtk-decoration-layout to be able to use the internal CSD.  
 On GNOME with `gsettings set org.gnome.desktop.wm.preferences button-layout 'icon:minimize,maximize,close'`.  
 Generally with editing your `~/.config/gtk-4.0/settings.ini` and/or `~/.config/gtk-3.0/settings.ini` and adding `gtk-decoration-layout=icon:minimize,maximize,close` in the `[Settings]` block.  
 The layout was only an example, it is up to preference, documentation is here: https://docs.gtk.org/gtk4/property.Settings.gtk-decoration-layout.html  
 
+### Global menu
+
+When the desktop shows application menus in a global menu, the library exports the main menu of GTK4 header bars to it, as appmenu-gtk-module does for GTK3.  
+GTK learns that from the `gtk-shell-shows-menubar` setting (`Gtk/ShellShowsMenubar` in XSETTINGS). When it is off, nothing is exported.  
+The menu is published through the `_GTK_*` window properties, which Unity, vala-panel-appmenu (Xfce, MATE, Budgie) and the GMenu proxy of KDE Plasma read on X11.  
+Items that embed a widget are left out. Items whose action is installed on a widget class cannot be activated over D-Bus, so they get a stand-in action on the window.  
+
 ### Flatpak
 
 The library can be used as is.
